      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "REGGAE MISS (6) flew the lids with a sensational early split and hit the frame with a 4 length third (28.80) over 500m at this track. Form is hard to fault from this box, with a win and five minor placings from six starts. Racing well and deserves a win. MIDNIGHT THUNDER (4) has a strong record here with four wins and two placings from 10 starts. In the money last time at Shepparton (25.82) in a Grade 5, finishing a long neck second. Looks one of the chances. ROCK ETERNAL (2) has been settling off the speed lately, finishing sixth (23.99) last time in a Mix 3/4 at Horsham. Solid record here at the distance winning three races. Comes out of a solid form race last start. Better than the latest run and deserves another chance. HALF MAC (1) is worth some thought after showing speed and filling a placing last start.",
